on":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":373635,"output_tokens":4399,"requests":10}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the new search path makes a malformed (non-dict) page FATAL given that the reused `_iter_cursor_pages` ends the walk quietly on a non-dict response — e.g. validate each yielded page's `issues` shape in the search consumer and raise + invalidate rather than relying on the shared helper, which treats a non-dict as a clean end-of-walk.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.13,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["acli_graph.py _iter_cursor_pages: 'A non-dict response ends the walk quietly — callers treat pages already yielded as the partial result.' (lines 65-67, 84-86)","Plan Approach: 'Reject malformed search responses; invalidate a partially failed search so a later attempt cannot silently reuse a truncated result.'","Plan: 'malformed responses and cursor stalls are fatal to that search/pass.'","The existing get_parent_map/get_comment_map readers accept the quiet partial (fail-open whole-project maps); the new per-JQL Done search is a top-N capped read where a silent short result reintroduces the bound-but-absent hazard (ADR 0028)."],"finding":"The plan mandates malformed search responses be rejected fatally ('Reject malformed search responses'; 'malformed responses and cursor stalls are fatal to that search/pass'), but the reused shared helper _iter_cursor_pages treats a non-dict response as a QUIET end-of-walk (`if not isinstance(resp, dict): return`), yielding the pages-so-far as a partial result. The plan does not say where/how the fatal-rejection policy is enforced relative to this quiet-return seam, so a malformed/non-dict page would silently truncate the Done search rather than fail loud.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8a8324a0616b071c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"loca